- The timing windows live in the item's units and must end at the audio's duration. An item that reuses another's audio needs units identical to the ones that audio was made from.
- Nothing deletes audio. If a delete is added, a shared file needs to know which items still use it.
- Shape settled "Clients see no change"; sharing audio between items is new behaviour beyond the migration.`));
