python3 - <<'EOF'
import json
src=open('/tmp/b2.mmd').read()
prose="""Nagara runs as three deployables and a shared package. Clients reach only the API Worker; the pipeline Worker has no public routes; the text-to-speech service stays on Modal.

The API Worker checks the API key and serves enqueue, poll, retry, audio, images and health. It writes the item row at enqueue, creates the item's Workflow instance and restarts it on retry through a binding to the pipeline Worker's Workflow by script name, and reads a running item's status from the instance. For audio and images it answers with a 307 to a presigned GET URL that it signs with its own R2 API token; branch 7 holds the detail.

The item Workflow does all the work for one item. It writes the finished state into the item row, a ledger row for each metered call it makes, and new recipe versions. It calls Firecrawl through its own fetch client, Gemini through AI Gateway to describe images, the Images binding for rasters, and Modal's two endpoints behind proxy auth, handing Modal a PUT URL that the pipeline Worker signs with its own R2 API token. Branch 5 holds its steps.

DomainQueue lets one item per domain extract at a time: the Workflow waits for its domain's lease and releases it after the recipe step.

The recipe runtime runs a domain's recipe against the fetched page. The Flue author and revision agents write a recipe or revise one, calling their model through AI Gateway.

common/ is a package both Workers build from: the shared types, the SQL migrations and the cassette replay library. Only its migrations are deployed."""
js=open('/tmp/b2-render.tpl','w') if False else None
open('/tmp/b2-data.json','w').write(json.dumps({'src':src,'prose':prose}))
EOF
