import json
d={
'out':open('/tmp/b3-out.mmd').read(),'modal':open('/tmp/b3-modal.mmd').read(),
'h1':'API Worker and item Workflow',
't1':"""Interface (through the cross-script Workflow binding)
| Member              | Answers                                    | Who asks                |
|---------------------|--------------------------------------------|-------------------------|
| create              | starts the item's instance                 | API Worker, at enqueue  |
| restart from a step | runs the instance again from the step      | API Worker, on retry    |
|                     | that failed                                |                         |
| status              | Cloudflare's state of a running instance   | API Worker, on poll     |

Inputs
| Input   | What it is          | Where it comes from     | Required |
|---------|---------------------|-------------------------|----------|
| item id | the item row's id   | API Worker, at enqueue  | Yes      |""",
'p1':"""The API Worker reaches the item Workflow only through the cross-script Workflow binding. At enqueue it writes the item row and then creates the instance with the item's id as its only param. The Workflow reads everything else from the row, and its first step writes the instance's own id into the row; until then a poll reports the item as queued. On retry the API Worker restarts the instance from the step that failed, with the same param, and on poll it reads a running item's status from the instance.

The Workflow writes the item's finished state into the row itself, and returns the article's title, its units and the extraction verdict as its output; the verdict is empty when extraction succeeded. The param and output types live in common/, next to the unit union, so both Workers build against the same shapes.""",
'h2':'item Workflow and Modal',
't2':"""Interface (HTTP, Modal proxy auth headers on every request)
| Member          | Answers                                   | Who asks                |
|-----------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------|
| start synthesis | accepts a synthesis and returns its call  | item Workflow           |
|                 | id                                        |                         |
| fetch result    | the call's result, or that it is not      | item Workflow, polling  |
|                 | ready yet                                 |                         |""",
'p2':"""The item Workflow reaches Modal over HTTP through two web endpoints, and every request carries Modal's proxy auth headers. A start request carries each unit's spoken form and the item's voice, as the Modal call does today, plus a destination URL: a presigned R2 PUT URL for the item's audio key, signed by the pipeline Worker. Modal uploads the finished audio there, and the Workflow polls the result endpoint until the result is ready.

The result carries one timing window per unit, the audio's duration and its format, and no audio bytes, which keeps it far below the 1 MiB a Workflow step can return. Modal accepts no idempotency key, so a start step that runs again after a deploy synthesizes a second time, and the second upload overwrites the same audio key. A result Modal no longer holds after 7 days keeps today's handling. Production and local development call the same Modal app."""}
