src=open('/tmp/b5.mmd').read()
prose="""The item Workflow does all the work for one item, in nine steps run in order. It is created with the item's id, reads the URL and the voice from the item row, and its first step writes the instance's id into the row. Every step runs inside one wrapper, which writes current_step and the status the step gives it as the step starts, clears the error, and writes failed with the error when the step's last attempt fails. fetch and lease give queued; every later step gives generating.

fetch gets the page through Firecrawl with our own fetch-based client. lease waits for the domain's lease from DomainQueue, so only one item per domain extracts at a time, and release hands it back as soon as recipe has run. recipe runs the domain's recipe through the deterministic runtime, with the Flue agents writing or revising a recipe when the domain needs one. images and describe process the article's images (branch 6). start synthesis hands Modal the spoken forms, the voice and a presigned PUT URL for the audio; poll asks Modal for the result until it is ready; store writes the finished state into the row.

Each step is retried up to 3 times and each attempt has its own timeout: fetch 2 min, lease 1 h, recipe 15 min, release 1 min, images 5 min, describe 5 min, start synthesis 2 min, each poll 1 min, store 1 min. A step that makes a metered call writes its ledger row. A deploy can run a step again; a synthesis started twice uploads twice to the same audio key. The Workflow returns no output; everything it produces is on the row.

A step that fails for good while the item holds the domain's lease, and a retry from lease or earlier while an earlier attempt still holds it, are handled the way the pipeline handles them today."""
